        <AlertDescription>
          <p>If you do not have access to the Red Hat Enterprise Linux CoreOS (RHCOS) images that were used to create your cluster, you can add more compute machines to your OpenShift Container Platform cluster with newer versions of Red Hat Enterprise Linux CoreOS (RHCOS) images. For instructions, see <a href="https://access.redhat.com/solutions/5514051">Adding new nodes to UPI cluster fails after upgrading to OpenShift 4.6+</a>.</p>
